# All calls go through the gateway (5200). Start first: dotnet run --project Micro.Launcher
@base = http://localhost:5200
@alice = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@bob = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### Health of all the services
GET {{base}}/health

### [Accounts] Get Alice
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}

### [Accounts] Withdraw 100 € → outbox → broker → Notifications
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 100 }

### [Transfers] Transfer from Alice to Bob → HTTP calls to Accounts, then event
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 250 }

### [Notifications] Alice (they arrive a few moments later: eventual consistency)
GET {{base}}/notifications/{{alice}}

### [Notifications] Bob
GET {{base}}/notifications/{{bob}}

### The internal API of Accounts is NOT exposed by the gateway (404)
POST {{base}}/internal/accounts/{{alice}}/debits
Content-Type: application/json

{ "operationId": "pirate", "amount": 1000 }

### Broker state (directly, without going through the gateway)
GET http://localhost:5209/state
